// `Main::main` cites the dependency's `establish` boundary axiom to satisfy
// its own `established()` postcondition, and the root accepts that claim with
// `Build::accept_boundary<establish>`. Once ordinary package review records
// the acceptance in `omega.lock`, the program should run and exit 0 with no
// other approval file. Without that acceptance it must ask for review; a
// dependency cannot approve itself. ADMISSIONS-FILE-DELETED owns this case.
//
// `omega --check` at 42db5b1ac3a rejects with "package-aware compilation
// cannot admit individual accepted machine `establish`; package claims
// require complete package-level review". Earlier, removing the acceptance
// for diagnosis reached stage 04's execution-planning refusal (boundary
// `establish` has no boundary plan): the citation needs an admitted
// fact-only invocation, not an invented executable provider.
use trusted_claims::claims;

data Main {}

machine Main::main()
ensures established()
{
    establish();
}
